# Shell scripts and the Containerfile must keep LF endings in the worktree, not only in the index.
# Windows checkouts here run with core.autocrlf=true, which gave every .sh a CRLF worktree copy.
# Git Bash's own bash tolerates that, so nothing complained — but the development container
# (scripts/devbox.sh) mounts this worktree and runs Linux bash over the same files, and that bash
# stops on the first line: `set: pipefail: invalid option name`, because the option it read was
# `pipefail\r`. A message that names nothing it is about.
#
# Adding the attribute is not enough on its own: a worktree that already holds CRLF copies keeps
# them until the files are checked out again (`git add --renormalize . && git checkout -- .`).
*.sh text eol=lf
Containerfile text eol=lf
